    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-058: `top: 50%` + `transform: translateY(-50%)`**. **Documentation only.** Implementation (~150 lines, 2 source files) lands in a follow-up PR.\n\n**Closes the 5-ADR magnifier chain**: 054 (diagnose) → 055 (bg color) → 056 (bg URL) → 057 (`parent_content_height`) → **058 (centering)**.\n\n## The magnifier chain status\n\n| ADR | Contribution | y-position |\n|---|---|---|\n| 054 | Diagnosed `top: 50%` + `translateY(-50%)`; shipped rotate | invisible |\n| 055 | `background:` color forms | invisible |\n| 056 | `background:` URL forms — **renders** | `y=7` (too high) |\n| 057 | `parent_content_height` threading | `y=7` |\n| **058** | **`top: 50%` + `translateY(-50%)`** | **`y=18` (centered)** |\n\n## The critical distinction\n\nTwo different `%` references, two independent layers:\n\n| Property | `%` reference | When resolved |\n|---|---|---|\n| `top: 50%` | **Parent** content height (`abs_ch`) | Layout time |\n| `translateY(-50%)` | **Own** box height | After `box.height` finalized |\n\n**The magnifier math**: `7 + (42 * 0.5) - (20 * 0.5) = 18` (centered).\n\nDifferent references → different resolution points → two independent code paths.\n\n## What ships (2 layers, ~150 lines)\n\n### Layer 1: `top: %` in absolute positioning\n\n- `abs_ctx.parent_content_height = abs_ch` (1 line)\n- Split `parse_off` into `parse_off_h` (left/right, width) and `parse_off_v` (top/bottom, height)\n- 4 call sites updated\n\n**`bottom: %` works for free** (same `parse_off_v` path).\n\n### Layer 2: `transform: translateY()` paint support\n\n- `LayoutBox::transform_translate_y = 0.0f`\n- Extract `translateY(...)` raw value before `box.height` known\n- Resolve after `box.height` set (`%` against own height, else `parse_length`)\n- Paint wrapper generalizes `did_rotate` → `did_transform` (rotate OR translate)\n\n## Design decisions\n\n**Two-block structure is required.** `top: %` resolves at layout time (parent height known when recursing into children). `translateY(-50%)` resolves after `box.height` finalized (own height known only after children). Attempting to resolve both at one point would either use the wrong reference or the wrong timing.\n\n**Translate-first-then-rotate in paint wrapper**, regardless of source order. Correct for the magnifier (translate-only). Combined `rotate + translate` source-order semantics deferred — no current fixture uses it.\n\n**`parse_off` split into `h`/`v` lambdas** (self-documenting at call sites) rather than a boolean parameter.\n\n## Visible delta (verified in implementation commit)\n\n**Synthetic fixture** (4 rows):\n- Control: 20px icon at container top (`y=0`)\n- `top: 50%` only: icon at `y=21` (half container, still wrong)\n- `translateY(-50%)` only: icon at `y=-10` (above container, worse)\n- **Both**: icon at `y=11` (perfectly centered)\n\n**Wikipedia production**: search magnifier at `y=18` (was `y=7`). **Definitive visual proof of the 5-ADR chain.**\n\n## Regression protections\n\n- `top: Npx` unchanged (routes through `parse_length_for_height` which delegates to `parse_length` for non-%)\n- Rotate-only unchanged (translate=0, no-op)\n- Existing absolute tests unchanged (`top: 10px` etc.)\n- Paint wrapper `did_transform` invariant preserved (save iff pop)\n- `transform_translate_y_raw` must be declared at function scope (survives from transform block to post-height resolution)\n\n## Deferred\n\n- `translateX()` / 2-arg `translate()` — not needed\n- Combined `rotate + translate` source-order semantics — no fixture\n- `bottom: %`, `left: %`, `right: %` — bottom works for free; left/right use width correctly\n- `translateY()` on non-absolute elements — works, no consumer\n\n## Test count target\n\n- 669 → ~676 (+7 tests, 1 flipped)\n\nRefs #254\n",
